     ttppmmrr — IEEE 802.1Q Two-Port MAC Relay interface

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ppsseeuuddoo--ddeevviiccee ttppmmrr

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ttppmmrr driver implements an 802.1Q (originally 802.1aj) Two-Port MAC
     Relay (TPMR).  A TPMR is a simplified Ethernet bridge with exactly two
     member ports, and it unconditionally relays Ethernet packets between
     those ports.

     ttppmmrr interfaces can be created at runtime using the iiffccoonnffiigg ttppmmrr_N ccrreeaattee
     command or by setting up a hostname.if(5) configuration file for
     netstart(8).

     Other forms of Ethernet bridging are available using the bridge(4) Ether‐
     net bridge driver and the veb(4) Virtual Ethernet Bridge device.  Link
     aggregation of Ethernet interfaces can be achieved using the aggr(4) and
     trunk(4) drivers.

